{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790400450,"nonce":"xlQ1SfN8kLoU6QxKox3WCyy9KPA=","title":"Std.isOfType / Type.* APIs cannot read a type held in a Dynamic; Int64 has no box tag (Issue4285, Issue4407, Issue4014)","message":"(1) Std.isOfType(v, t) with t a Dynamic value desugars to TypeCheck{expected: static type of arg 2}; for Dynamic, runtime_type_id returns 5 (TYPE_STRING). A class/enum passed as Dynamic is a haxe_box_reference_ptr box carrying the id -- read it at runtime. (2) Type.createEnum/getEnumName take an I64 enum id; a Dynamic enum type passes the box pointer (runtime_mapping.rs). Also create_enum_value copies boxed args into typed enum fields without unboxing, and enum_eq compares boxed params by pointer. (3) Int64 is a native i64 boxed with TYPE_INT, so isInt64(dyn) compares 3 with the ___Int64 class hash. Probes: scratch triage-h/i4285, i4407, i4407b, i4014.","files":null}]}